s a function of the variable $s$ defined as\n\n$$\nF(s)=L{f(t)}={\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }{e}^{-st}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t\n$$\n\nprovided that this integral exists and is finite. \n\nFor the function $f(t)={e}^{7t},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(s) & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }{e}^{-st}\\cdot {e}^{7t}\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }{e}^{-st+7t}\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }{e}^{(7-s)t}\\text{d}t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe calculate our integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(s) & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }{e}^{(7-s)t}\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={lim}_{a\\to \\infty }{\\int }_{0}^{a}{e}^{(7-s)t}\\text{d}t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo evaluate the last integral, we must consider whether $s\\ne 7$ or $s=7.$\n\n- If $s\\ne 7,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(s) & ={lim}_{a\\to \\infty }{\\int }_{0}^{a}{e}^{(7-s)t}\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={lim}_{a\\to \\infty }{(\\frac{1}{7-s}{e}^{(7-s)t})|}_{0}^{a} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{7-s}({lim}_{a\\to \\infty }{e}^{(7-s)a}-1) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{s-7}(1-{lim}_{a\\to \\infty }{e}^{(7-s)a}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{s-7}-\\frac{1}{s-7}\\cdot {lim}_{a\\to \\infty }{e}^{(7-s)a}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet's evaluate the limit. We have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{a\\to \\infty }{e}^{(7-s)a}={\\begin{aligned}0,\\, & s>7, \\\\ \\infty ,\\, & s<7.\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- If $s=7,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(7) & ={lim}_{a\\to \\infty }{\\int }_{0}^{a}{e}^{(7-7)t}\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={lim}_{a\\to \\infty }{\\int }_{0}^{a}{e}^{0t}\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={lim}_{a\\to \\infty }{\\int }_{0}^{a}\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={lim}_{a\\to \\infty }t\\,{|}_{0}^{a} \\\\  & ={lim}_{a\\to \\infty }(a-0) \\\\  & ={lim}_{a\\to \\infty }a \\\\  & =\\infty .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore:\n\n- For $s\\le 7$ the integral is divergent.\n\n- For $s>7$ the integral is convergent.\n\nEvaluating for $s>7,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(s) & =\\frac{1}{s-7}-\\frac{1}{s-7}\\cdot {lim}_{a\\to \\infty }{e}^{(7-s)a} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{s-7}-\\frac{1}{s-7}\\cdot 0 \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{s-7}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the Laplace transform of $f(t)={e}^{7t}$ is $F(s)=\\frac{1}{s-7},$ defined for $s>7.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186318967 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a2fd0466-9f47-5adc-911a-f297858951b1" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating Laplace Transforms of Real Exponential Functions"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "86a26809-f2e8-543e-98c3-76b5b7bfa8d0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }{e}^{(1/4+s)t}\\,\\text{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186318969} {:answer/id #uuid "44d4d2e8-c35f-5be1-be93-177db6e8ccc3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }{e}^{(1/4-s)t}\\,\\text{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186318970} {:answer/id #uuid "f2314f12-64b5-57b0-897d-e81d40884610" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{-\\infty }^{\\infty }{e}^{(1/4-s)t}\\,\\text{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186318971} {:answer/id #uuid "d36b7ae2-aef2-501c-85e4-e300a2d6b6ec" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{-\\infty }^{\\infty }{e}^{(1/4+s)t}\\,\\text{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186318972}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "44d4d2e8-c35f-5be1-be93-177db6e8ccc3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }{e}^{(1/4-s)t}\\,\\text{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186318970} :answer-field/id #uuid "ac8beaef-0738-5c58-85d9-0a540d390e02" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186318968} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b21afe72-22d3-5501-8f37-91ed8172d6f3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "s>\\frac{1}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186318974} {:answer/id #uuid "8eb34eb4-55c9-5b6a-a818-b8e0e2708a71" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "s\\ge \\frac{1}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186318975} {:answer/id #uuid "947d8960-6d34-5e38-